<%- include("partials/head", {
  title: "Bulk Beef — Quarters, Halves & Wholes | Tui Farms, Manheim PA",
  description: "Buy beef by the quarter, half, or whole from Tui Farms in Manheim, Lancaster County PA — priced by hanging weight, cut to your own cut sheet by our local butcher. Text 717-803-1649 to reserve."
}) %>
<%- include("partials/nav") %>
<%- include("partials/page-title", {
  heading: "🧊 Bulk Beef — Quarters, Halves & Wholes",
  subheading: "Fill the freezer once at our best price per pound"
}) %>

<section class="page-section" style="max-width:860px;">

  <!-- Intro -->
  <p style="text-align:center; max-width:38em; margin:0 auto 1.5em;">
    Filling a freezer once beats shopping for beef every week — and buying by
    the quarter, half, or whole is the best per-pound price we offer, on every
    single cut.
  </p>

  <!-- The value bomb -->
  <div class="bulk-callout">
    Every pound of the animal costs the same — filet mignon included. All-in,
    most bulk orders land around <strong>$10 per packaged pound</strong>; that
    same filet runs <strong>$38/lb</strong> by the package.
  </div>

  <!-- How it works -->
  <h2 style="color:var(--primary); text-align:center; margin:1.6em 0 0.8em;">How it works</h2>
  <ol class="bulk-steps">
    <li>
      <h3>Reserve</h3>
      <p>
        Text <strong>717-803-1649</strong> and tell us quarter, half, or whole.
        We'll give you the timeline and sort out the details by text.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:0;">
        <a class="btn" href="<%= reserveHref %>">Text to reserve</a>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Your cut sheet</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom:0;">
        You decide what your beef becomes: steak thickness, roast sizes, how
        much ground. Never done one? It takes about 10 minutes and we'll walk
        you through every choice. (Buying a quarter? You'll share one cut sheet
        with the other quarter on your half — see the note below.)
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Drop-off &amp; the farm payment</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom:0;">
        We take your animal to our local butcher. Once it's weighed, your
        payment to Tui Farms is due — the per-pound price times the
        <strong>hanging weight</strong> (the butcher-ready weight; you'll know
        the exact number before you pay).
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Pick up at the butcher</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom:0;">
        The butcher cuts, vacuum-packs, and freezes everything to your cut
        sheet. When it's ready, you pick it up there and pay their butchering
        bill directly — figure about <strong>$1.25/lb hanging weight</strong>
        for a straightforward cut sheet, a bit more for extras like patties or
        beef sticks.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <!-- Pricing -->
  <div class="card" style="margin:2em 0;">
    <h3 style="color:var(--primary); margin-top:0;">What it costs</h3>
    <p>
      Bulk beef is priced on <strong>hanging weight</strong> — roughly 55–60%
      of it comes home as packaged cuts.
    </p>
    <table class="pricing-table">
      <tr>
        <td>Quarter — about 200 lbs hanging, ~110 lbs of cuts</td>
        <td><strong>$4.75/lb</strong> hanging</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Half — about 400 lbs hanging, ~225 lbs of cuts</td>
        <td><strong>$4.60/lb</strong> hanging</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Whole — about 800 lbs hanging, ~450 lbs of cuts</td>
        <td><strong>$4.50/lb</strong> hanging</td>
      </tr>
    </table>
    <p style="margin-bottom:0.4em;">
      <strong>A note on quarters:</strong> the butcher cuts down to halves, so
      two quarters share one half — both quarter orders use the same cut sheet,
      and we split the packed beef into two shares as equal as we can make
      them.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-bottom:0.4em;">
      <strong>A worked example:</strong> a whole beef hanging at 800 lbs is
      $3,600 to the farm, plus a butchering bill around $1,000 paid to the
      butcher at pickup — about $4,600 all-in for roughly 450 lbs of cuts,
      or right around $10 per packaged pound.
    </p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:0;">
      Two payments: the farm (right after drop-off, once the hanging weight is
      known) and the butcher (at pickup). Every animal weighs a little
      different — your totals go by the real numbers.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Freezer guide -->
  <div class="card" style="margin:2em 0;">
    <h3 style="color:var(--primary); margin-top:0;">Will it fit?</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>A quarter</strong> takes about 4 cubic feet — a mini chest
      freezer, or a mostly-empty kitchen freezer, handles it.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>A half</strong> takes about 7 cubic feet — a small chest freezer
      swallows it with room to spare.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-bottom:0;">
      <strong>A whole</strong> takes about 13 cubic feet — a standard full-size
      chest freezer handles it comfortably.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- What you get -->
  <div class="card" style="margin:2em 0;">
    <h3 style="color:var(--primary); margin-top:0;">What you get</h3>
    <p style="margin-bottom:0;">
      Roughly half comes back as ground and everyday beef, and the rest as
      steaks and roasts — and your cut sheet shifts that balance whichever way
      your family eats.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%- include("partials/order-info") %>
</section>

<style>
  /* ---- bulk page (only this page uses these) ---- */
  .bulk-callout {
    background: var(--card-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 5px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.1em 1.3em;
    font-size: 1.12em;
    max-width: 34em;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .bulk-steps {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .bulk-steps li {
    counter-increment: step;
    position: relative;
    background: var(--card-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.1em 1.3em 1.1em 4em;
    margin-bottom: 1em;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
  }
  .bulk-steps li::before {
    content: counter(step);
    position: absolute;
    left: 1.1em;
    top: 1.1em;
    width: 1.9em;
    height: 1.9em;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--primary);
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 700;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .bulk-steps h3 { color: var(--primary); margin: 0 0 0.3em; }
</style>

<%- include("partials/footer") %>
